<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<opml version="2.0" xmlns:porridge="https://github.com/alexjj/porridge">
  <head>
    <title>2026</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <outline text="November 2026" type="calendarMonth" date="2026-11">
      <outline text="25th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-25">
        <outline text="I'm not too proud to back-fill entries in Porridge when I miss the chance to enter something on the day of." created="Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:10:14 GMT"/>
        <outline text="[Instinctive Chords app](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/instinctive-chords/id6445869486?mt=12)&lt;!-- {&quot;preview&quot;:&quot;true&quot;} --&gt;" created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:00:01 GMT">
          <outline text="Bought this for $4.99 to decode chords as I play them on a MIDI keyboard. It is wonderful and the developer has a level of taste that these apps usually don't exhibit." created="Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:04:27 GMT"/>
          <outline text="![Instinctive Chords app recognizing an F-sharp minor chord inversion](/images/2026/11/cleanshot-20261126130420-26130631.webp)"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="[Pierre Piscitelli](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8xhBnui4Hic) makes refreshingly non-hectic videos about how to play keyboard parts. So friendly and thorough." created="Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:03:47 GMT"/>
        <outline text="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8xhBnui4Hic" created="Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:07:30 GMT"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="24th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-24">
        <outline text="Dropped off assorted Matchbox, Lego, and other-brand police cars and various other car toys at the Angel Tree pickup for the kids we adopted as a web team. I wanted to get everything at Target, but they are low on police cars there. Had to fall back to Amazon for sheer breadth of options and speed of delivery." created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:36:55 GMT"/>
        <outline text="I’m sticking with Bear for daily notes and non-sensitive journal-type entries for now, but I have to admit it is indeed a kludge for those purposes. Other than the app-written metadata, there’s no concept of a proper “date” being attached to each note. I don’t know why I would let that bother me when I used Markdown text files for all this for so long before. The whole point of getting out of Obsidian was to make things dumber, less fiddly, and less customized, which I have sort of done. I need to learn to leave things alone. What’s that thing that Sarah always says about finding something that works and trusting it for a while? Sometimes I want tabs, folders, sections and pages (OneNote), sometimes I want something more flat with tags (Bear, The Archive), and sometimes I want just a linear record of random things (OBTF, Porridge). Usually I just want all three scenarios." created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:53:02 GMT"/>
        <outline text="The new YouTube embed feature in [Porridge](https://github.com/alexjj/porridge) is great!" created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:53:03 GMT"/>
        <outline text="[McCoy Tyner](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McCoy_Tyner) was born in 1938. He was almost 23 when he played on *Coltrane &quot;Live&quot; at the Village Vanguard*. He was almost 22 when they recorded *My Favorite Things*!" created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:53:04 GMT"/>
        <outline text="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EeEfoYHUdaM" created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:05:47 GMT"/>
        <outline text="My dudes keep adding songs for us to play on Black Friday night. I’m going to have to actually learn the keyboard to Toto’s “Hold The Line” properly over the next three days." created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:53:05 GMT"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="23rd November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-23">
        <outline text="I am so very tired of scrambling to do every little or big thing in my life at the last possible minute. You would think I'd get better at all of it as I get older, but nope. I make the lists, I capture the ideas and the to-dos into the lists, I set the reminders, but all of those things scream for attention from wherever they've been deposited. And when I revisit them, the squeakiest of them says to me, &quot;You better get to me right now, because there's never gonna be time if you don't do it right the F now.&quot;" created="Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:54:57 GMT"/>
        <outline text="I know Muse is the devil, but I set it up today to go to our cafeteria’s website every Monday at 11am, find and download this week’s PDF menu, and email it to me. Zero code. 👀" created="Tue, 24 Nov 2026 05:00:32 GMT"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="22nd November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-22">
        <outline text="[Quiche](https://quiche.industries/browser/) is a nice browser alternative in iOS. I've set it up with bookmarks for all eight of the blogs and wikis that [Jack](https://baty.net/) and [Alex](https://fondoftea.com/) post to." created="Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:59:31 GMT"/>
        <outline text="[Coding Agents Copy Your Secrets to a Hidden File. Thousands Are on GitHub — apiiro.com](https://apiiro.com/blog/coding-agents-leaking-secrets-github-dont-ask-again)" created="Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:36:30 GMT">
          <outline text="&gt; Ask Claude Code to check a database or call an API, and the command it proposes carries the secret from your config file. It asks before running it. Pick &quot;Yes, and don't ask again&quot; and it saves that exact command, secret included, to `.claude/settings.local.json` inside the project folder. Nothing in the repo marks that file as private, so it gets committed with the rest of the code." created="Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:45:51 GMT"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="I think I want to bring my drums home from Tim’s and put them in our basement." created="Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:47:48 GMT">
          <outline text="Could I get really quiet cymbals for less than just buying a full electronic kit? Could I add soundproofing above and beside the drums to keep them from shaking the house, knowing that sound-deadening heads can only do so much? Can I peel the black wraps off the Pearl Export shells and sand them down? Is there anything to see under there or would it be ugly?"/>
          <outline text="Turns out you can! The wood isn't much to look at, but it's better than the black lacquer wraps they came with. "/>
          <outline text="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=chlXeYk1S-M" created="Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:58:54 GMT"/>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="21st November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-21">
        <outline text="Kicking the tires. This is nice and it reminds me of something... 🥁" created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:24:51 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Listening to The Cakekitchen's [Time Flowing Backwards](https://thecakekitchen.bandcamp.com/album/time-flowing-backwards) after having gone down a Graeme Jefferies rabbit hole while stuck in the Atlanta airport during The Great Ground Stop of 2026. ![The Cakekitchen: Time Flowing Backwards](/images/2026/11/a2894995489-10-21113905.jpg)" created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:26:42 GMT"/>
        <outline text="[Camper](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/camper-for-bandcamp/id6822102958) is such a better iOS app for listening to Bandcamp than the Bandcamp app." created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:29:18 GMT"/>
        <outline text="I took the X100T on the trip to my work conference in Orlando and didn’t use it because I was gonna buy an SD card at a nearby Target, but getting to that Target would have required getting a Lyft/Uber and there was no way I would do that after the harrowing cab ride from the airport to Walt Disney World Dolphin Resort. I don’t know what I was thinking. There wasn’t time to shoot much amidst the conference sessions and having meals with people. So I lugged around a useless camera through the airports. Note to self: Now that I have to carry a CPAP, give up and get rolling luggage." created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:01:13 GMT"/>
        <outline text="[Denis Volkov: Task Workflow in Bear Notes](https://medium.com/productivity-heaven/task-workflow-in-bear-notes-517b1fbc4d59) – I never would have thought of putting a date search like `bear://x-callback-url/search?term=2024–04–20` in a Bear daily note, but this is a great idea." created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:04:02 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Still playing with Alex's cool new [Porridge](https://github.com/alexjj/porridge) blogging app. My first re-sync of my fork to his is giving me errors. I'm reaching the limits of what I know about GitHub, but it's sort of fun to get in the weeds with." created="Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:42:19 GMT"/>
      </outline>
    </outline>
  </body>
</opml>
